Trading the analytically-continued sinh-Gordon coupling for a real
parameter $\theta_0$, the staircase S-matrix is
\begin{equation}
S(\theta)=
\tanh\left(\frac{\theta{-}\theta_0}{2}-\frac{i\pi}{4}\right)
\tanh\left(\frac{\theta{+}\theta_0}{2}-\frac{i\pi}{4}\right) \end{equation}
and this leads to the following TBA equations for the pseudoenergy 
$\epsilon(\theta)$ for the system on a circle of circumference $R$\,:
\begin{equation}
\epsilon(\theta)=r\cosh\theta-\int_{{\mathbb R}}\phi_S(\theta-\theta')L(\theta')d\theta' \end{equation}
where $r=M\!R$, and
\begin{equation}
L(\theta)=\ln(1+e^{-\epsilon(\theta)})\,,\quad
\phi_S(\theta)=-\frac{i}{2\pi}\frac{d}{d\theta}\ln S(\theta)\,.
\end{equation}

The ground state energy of the system is then given by
$E(R)=-\frac{\pi}{6R}\,c_{\rm eff}(r)$, where the effective central charge
$c_{\rm eff}(r)$ is
\begin{equation}
c_{\rm eff}(r)=\frac{6}{\pi^2}\int_{{\mathbb R}}r\cosh(\theta)L(\theta)\,d\theta\,.
\end{equation}

For later use we define
\begin{equation}
(x)(\theta)=
\frac
{\sinh\left(\fract{\theta}{2}+\fract{i\pi x}{2}\right)}
{\sinh\left(\fract{\theta}{2}-\fract{i\pi x}{2}\right)}~,\qquad
\phi_{(x)}(\theta)=-\frac{i}{2\pi}\frac{d}{d\theta}\ln\,(x)(\theta)=
\frac{-\sin(\pi x)/(2\pi)\,}{\cosh(\theta)-\cos(\pi x)}~,
\end{equation}
and also
\begin{equation}
\phi(\theta)=-\phi_{(\frac{1}{2})}(\theta)=\frac{1}{2\pi\cosh(\theta)} \end{equation}
so that the staircase kernel $\phi_S(\theta)$ is
\begin{equation}
\phi_S(\theta)=\phi(\theta-\theta_0)+\phi(\theta+\theta_0)\,. \end{equation}

Indexing the
steps by an integer $m=3$, $4$ \dots, the 
